      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2011 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "We report the case of a 72-year-old woman with a fish bone-induced granulation tissue in the gastric wall that was initially diagnosed as a submucosal tumor by panendoscopy. High-frequency endoscopic ultrasonography identified the linear calcified fish bone embedded in a heterogeneous mass."
